mes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify (in the plan) that the pairwise-gap-over-bank-points measurement equals the policy's per-criterion current_evidence_steps<=3 boundary despite _sync_current resetting on criterion-became-current and multiple criteria potentially banking in one response — or re-denominate the oracle per-criterion (origin = prior bank == criterion-became-current) rather than global-cumulative pairwise.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3022,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["completion_tool_policy.py:147-153 _sync_current resets current_evidence_steps to empty set whenever _first_unbanked changes, so the per-criterion counter's origin is criterion-became-current","_bounded_bank_gaps computes gaps = [points[0], *(later-earlier for pairwise(points))] — origin of each gap is the PREVIOUS BANK, not the point the criterion became current","A batched evidence response or a multi-criterion record can bank several criteria at once, collapsing multiple 'gaps' onto one response and making len(gaps)==expected_criteria hold only if each bank lands in a distinct response"],"finding":"The response-denominated oracle reconstructs the policy's per-criterion evidence boundary from GLOBAL distinct executed-evidence run_steps taken pairwise between consecutive BANK points, but the production policy resets current_evidence_steps when a criterion becomes CURRENT (_sync_current at completion_tool_policy.py:147-153), whose origin is 'previous criterion banked', not 'previous point in the pairwise sequence' — and multiple criteria can bank within a single evidence/record response. The plan asserts this equivalence ('matching max_evidence_responses=3') without justifying that pairwise-gap-over-bank-points equals the policy's per-criterion response count.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f930b5faedd2415d4","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'The existing make_observed_upsert observer ... _bounded_bank_gaps keeps its exact shape ... over response-denominated points, matching max_evidence_responses=3'","norm_id":"ne05083e49ef840d3","priority":0.2978,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A model banks two criteria from evidence gathered across the same set of responses, or a criterion becomes current several responses before the model starts reading for it","A trial the policy itself would accept (each criterion within its own 3-response budget) is REJECTED by the pairwise-gap oracle, or vice-versa"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Consider (and record why chosen-vs-not) an alternative that asserts on the policy's own fail-closed output — bounded-fallback insufficiency records (evidence_sufficient=False) at the boundary — rather than reconstructing consumed evidence responses via an outer counting toolset, since the former measures the 0707 safety property directly and is immune to run_step-attribution drift.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["completion_tool_policy.py:186-192 fires policy.fallback_record(target_id, BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE) precisely at evidence_count >= max_evidence_responses — this is the observable boundary event","make_observed_upsert already inspects source and forwards evidence_sufficient/seeded kwargs, so the fail-closed marker is already visible at the upsert seam without adding an outer toolset"],"finding":"The plan reconstructs the policy's INPUT (evidence responses consumed) via an outer counting toolset, but a structurally-different and more contract-faithful alternative is not considered: assert directly on the policy's own fail-closed OUTPUT — the bounded-fallback INSUFFICIENCY records (met=false carrying evidence_sufficient=False / BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE, completion_tool_policy.py:55-59,190-191) that the policy banks exactly when a criterion exhausts its 3-response budget. Measuring the actual safety signal (no criterion banked via bounded-fallback; all banked from real evidence) is robust to the reset/gap-origin subtlety in the response-counting approach and is closer to what the 0707 oracle exists to protect.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f073c3aa850709e1f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / measurement seam paragraph","norm_id":"ndd47ea9a9cab8e52","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The response-counting wrapper mis-attributes a run_step (e.g. steered-then-executed within one step, or an evidence result that coincidentally equals a notice string) and drifts from the true boundary the fallback records mark"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the counting predicate as EXACT-equality against only COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE and ALL_CRITERIA_BANKED_NOTICE (not a substring test), and state explicitly that a BOUNDED_FALLBACK_NOTICE-suffixed result counts as an executed evidence response.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.601,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["completion_tool_policy.py:186-193 returns f'{result}\\n\\n{BOUNDED_FALLBACK_NOTICE}' for an EXECUTED evidence call at the boundary","Plan names only two of three notice constants defined at :46/:51/:60","The distinction (exact-equality on the two notices vs. substring match that would also catch the fallback text) is load-bearing for the counter's correctness"],"finding":"The plan's evidence-response counting rule enumerates only COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE and ALL_CRITERIA_BANKED_NOTICE as 'steered-not-executed' sentinels, but the inner policy also returns BOUNDED_FALLBACK_NOTICE appended to a real executed result (f'{result}\\n\\n{BOUNDED_FALLBACK_NOTICE}' at completion_tool_policy.py:192); an implementer using naive membership/containment against the notice set could mis-classify a fallback-fired executed call as not-counted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f92c50503c84cbab1","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'a result equal to COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE/ALL_CRITERIA_BANKED_NOTICE ... means steered-not-executed and is not counted'","norm_id":"nae1df28dab2e77e6","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A trial where a criterion's third evidence response fires the bounded fallback; that response executed and must count toward the >3 gap check"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State the rule as: count the run_step iff result != COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE and result != ALL_CRITERIA_BANKED_NOTICE (exact equality); a result containing BOUNDED_FALLBACK_NOTICE is an executed evidence response and IS counted.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify whether the oracle's evidence-response points are per-criterion (reset at each criterion boundary, mirroring _sync_current) or cumulative-global, and show the pairwise-gap<=3 formulation is equivalent to the enforcement's per-criterion max_evidence_responses=3 bound.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5827,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["completion_tool_policy.py:147-153 _sync_current RESETS current_evidence_steps to a fresh set whenever the first-unbanked id changes","completion_tool_policy.py:182-183 evidence_count = len(current_evidence_steps) is a PER-CRITERION count, not a global run_step total","Plan keeps _bounded_bank_gaps 'exact shape (points, pairwise gaps, all gaps <= 3)' — a pairwise-gap-of-monotonic-global-counter model, which mirrors the enforcement only if response points also reset/align per criterion"],"finding":"The plan asserts its response-denominated gap oracle 'matches max_evidence_responses=3' but does not specify whether the oracle's per-criterion response points reset per criterion, whereas the enforcement it mirrors resets its evidence-step set on every criterion change (_sync_current clears current_evidence_steps). Counting distinct global ctx.run_step values monotonically and taking pairwise gaps is not obviously equivalent to the enforcement's per-criterion bounded set.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1eb64b1684f6de69","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'records the distinct ctx.run_step values ... _bounded_bank_gaps keeps its exact shape ... over response-denominated points, matching max_evidence_responses=3'","norm_id":"n11898d59994c1c8c","priority":0.1173,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A criterion banked after 2 evidence responses followed by a criterion needing 3 more responses — the enforcement treats each per-criterion, but a global monotonic pairwise-gap oracle must produce the same accept/reject decision"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4444,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","